00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:32.330
Hey, Everett

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.160
What am I {like }in your world?

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.960
Let me take a look

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:40.460
Hey, Everett

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:44.250
According to you, there are lots of different worlds

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:47.260
I'm not sure I understand

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:49.220
"Hi, Dandy"

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:51.140
"Hello"

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:53.220
"How are you doing?"

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:56.220
Hey, Ph.D.

00:22:56.220 --> 00:23:00.060
Your alternate worlds will always overlap and never interfere

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:02.730
That blows my mind

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:08.900
Things get harder when they cool

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:12.910
Things melt when they're heated

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:15.120
This world is so full of rules,

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.750
it's going to drive me crazy

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:23.080
One dimension, two dimensions, three dimensions

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:27.050
A supernova is spreading from west to east

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:29.760
Easy game, easy game,

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:31.220
too easy game

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:35.760
The way there is fine, but what about coming back?

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:40.690
A dream of a never-ending dream

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:45.020
A wonderful, milky kiss

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:52.110
Will this universe expand forever?

